(6316497, 934537, 23098, '<td valign="top">One of my favorites in the challenge.  Like your interpretation with this shot.  Processing is stellar.</td>', 'One of my favorites in the challenge.  Like your interpretation with this shot.  Processing is stellar.', '2011-02-16 08:15:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6316499, 933581, 10785, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by EL-ROI:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice arrangement! I like the graduation of the colors. More technical and precise people would have had all of the pencil labels lined up or not shown at all. I am guessing a wider aperture was used... f3.5, f4?? I may be wrong but it looks like the focal point is not quite on the circle. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Had to revisit this one to see what caused the blur. I now see it is not the f stop but it was the shutter speed. 1/25 hand held probably. Very slow shutter to use handheld. I have heard that the rule of thumb for handholding a shot is 1/focal length. So for a 50mm lens your longest shutter speed hand held should be about 1/50. Keep on shooting!</td>', 'Originally posted by EL-ROI: Nice arrangement! I like the graduation of the colors. More technical and precise people would have had all of the pencil labels lined up or not shown at all. I am guessing a wider aperture was used... f3.5, f4?? I may be wrong but it looks like the focal point is not quite on the circle.   Had to revisit this one to see what caused the blur. I now see it is not the f stop but it was the shutter speed. 1/25 hand held probably. Very slow shutter to use handheld. I have heard that the rule of thumb for handholding a shot is 1/focal length. So for a 50mm lens your longest shutter speed hand held should be about 1/50. Keep on shooting!', '2011-02-16 08:17:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6316504, 933776, 10785, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by EL-ROI:</b></div><hr/><i> Looks like a shot of an animal claw mark, or Wolverine from X-Men. It makes me think it was chasing something like a crowd of people and it left it''s mark as everything raced for the exit. Posthumous Worthy??? We''ll see. <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> Fascinating interruption of language. I like your title.<br/> <br/>This goes into my fantasy art gallery.<br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//blackyak.com/dpc/artpost.jpg'', strrpos(''//blackyak.com/dpc/artpost.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//blackyak.com/dpc/artpost.jpg"/> </i></td></tr></table></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sure enough!!</td>', 'Originally posted by EL-ROI: Looks like a shot of an animal claw mark, or Wolverine from X-Men. It makes me think it was chasing something like a crowd of people and it left it''s mark as everything raced for the exit. Posthumous Worthy??? We''ll see. Originally posted by posthumous: Fascinating interruption of language. I like your title. This goes into my fantasy art gallery.    Sure enough!!', '2011-02-16 08:21:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6316513, 933824, 114225, '<td valign="top">Hi roni, I see you are new here. I notice in your comments you said you "painted" the bird yellow. While there are some legal way to do this in basic editing (depending on the scene), this one strikes me as a time when a local edit was made. Notice that this is a Basic Editing challenge, so if someone had requested validation of your image and you did use a local edit, your image would have been DQed. Just a heads up!</td>', 'Hi roni, I see you are new here. I notice in your comments you said you "painted" the bird yellow. While there are some legal way to do this in basic editing (depending on the scene), this one strikes me as a time when a local edit was made. Notice that this is a Basic Editing challenge, so if someone had requested validation of your image and you did use a local edit, your image would have been DQed. Just a heads up!', '2011-02-16 08:27:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6316532, 934537, 67697, '<td valign="top">The Ooobie just re-started and look at you, already an Oobie ribbon hog :)  Congrats!  And I love the photo - it''s a joyful shot.</td>', 'The Ooobie just re-started and look at you, already an Oobie ribbon hog :)  Congrats!  And I love the photo - it''s a joyful shot.', '2011-02-16 08:44:01.000000', NULL, 0),
