(6317290, 934300, 20168, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scrybz:</b></div><hr/><i> if you managed to do this without breaking "basic editing" rules, I want a tutorial! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No tutorial needed for not breaking "basic editing" rules in submitting monochromatic photos. I''m the one who needs a tutorial for getting photos off my camera without creating a DQ-able "copy". <br/> <br/>Editing Steps: <br/>1) took photo of monochromatic surface (back of a spiral notebook)<br/>2) hue shifted to blue<br/>3) saturation increased for intensity<br/>4) noise reduced<br/>5) square crop<br/>6) resized to 800x800<br/>7) submitted<br/>8) DQd. <br/>Note: No basic rules were injured or killed in the shooting of this animal.</td>', 'Originally posted by scrybz: if you managed to do this without breaking "basic editing" rules, I want a tutorial!   No tutorial needed for not breaking "basic editing" rules in submitting monochromatic photos. I''m the one who needs a tutorial for getting photos off my camera without creating a DQ-able "copy".  Editing Steps: 1) took photo of monochromatic surface (back of a spiral notebook)2) hue shifted to blue3) saturation increased for intensity4) noise reduced5) square crop6) resized to 800x8007) submitted8) DQd. Note: No basic rules were injured or killed in the shooting of this animal.', '2011-02-16 16:14:01.000000', NULL, 0),
